2026-01-12 23:03:04 | INFO | "./webui\batch_video_generator.py:98": generate_single_video - task.start completed with result: {'videos': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\96c062f7-95ab-4639-ac7f-917a948b2270\\final-1.mp4'], 'combined_videos': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\96c062f7-95ab-4639-ac7f-917a948b2270\\combined-1.mp4'], 'script': "Focus on nutrient-dense, easy-to-digest foods that can combat treatment side effects and support your body's healing journey. Opt for lean proteins like grilled chicken, fish, or tofu to aid in tissue repair and maintain muscle mass; small, frequent meals of scrambled eggs, yogurt, or cottage cheese can also be easier to tolerate if appetite is low. Incorporate soft, cooked vegetables such as steamed carrots, pureed sweet potatoes, or mashed zucchini for essential vitamins and fiber, and blend fruits like bananas, berries, or peaches into smoothies for a gentle source of energy and antioxidants. Hydration is paramount, so sip on water, clear broths, herbal teas, or diluted juices throughout the day to prevent dehydration and alleviate mouth sores. Prioritize bland, simple foods to manage nausea and taste changes often experienced during chemotherapy. Think about creamy options like oatmeal, rice pudding, or plain pasta; these are gentle on the stomach and provide much-needed carbohydrates for energy. If certain smells trigger nausea, try cold foods or room temperature meals as they tend to have less odor. Consider small portions of plain crackers, toast, or pretzels as a safe bet when feeling queasy, and experiment with mild flavorings like ginger or mint, which can sometimes help settle an upset stomach. Embrace foods that offer comfort and sustenance without overwhelming your senses. Listen to your body and adapt your diet as needed, recognizing that individual responses to chemotherapy vary greatly. Some days may call for heartier meals, while others might necessitate only liquids or small, bland snacks. Don't hesitate to discuss dietary concerns and potential supplements with your healthcare team or a registered dietitian; they can offer personalized guidance to ensure you're getting the nutrition you need. Remember, nourishing yourself is an act of strength and resilience during this challenging time, and every bite contributes to your body's fight and recovery.", 'terms': ['healthy food', 'patient eating', 'recovery food', 'nourishment'], 'audio_file': 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\96c062f7-95ab-4639-ac7f-917a948b2270\\audio.mp3', 'audio_duration': 123, 'subtitle_path': 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\96c062f7-95ab-4639-ac7f-917a948b2270\\subtitle.srt', 'materials': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-fef617d321773e8a90c6d613bcd98e45.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-73a4a6fad01b97a48136af2f94559d51.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-25e53b78d5ea9f889d22c69de63df724.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-32da78b88e33859d9506aa8c90e798b1.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-4b9ca0e3b2481cb1339ec5ecfa894588.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-0b9d94c3c601309b982be3e4f37cf285.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-76ada77b1b471b04049d08d2f4591090.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-f5c2b9d0331179cef21fd149ec86c166.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-19cbc8dce0abe1b7bcc9cda776658681.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-55c3d581d94821cff6836e1c140249c9.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-407ae1f52258ce2ec7008c10ea850ab1.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-e36638e73aeb40f1a2a0768f6e93db70.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-e96ed55a2b11e39dbae846bbd4960a45.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\sto