2026-01-14 21:29:25 | INFO | "./webui\batch_video_generator.py:98": generate_single_video - task.start completed with result: {'videos': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\1993e61e-2405-41d7-b177-859dcc1cdd23\\final-1.mp4'], 'combined_videos': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\1993e61e-2405-41d7-b177-859dcc1cdd23\\combined-1.mp4'], 'script': "Diabetes is terrifying not just because of the daily management of blood sugar levels, but because of the insidious way it can silently steal your health. Imagine your body's delicate balance thrown into chaos, leading to a constant internal struggle. High blood sugar acts like a slow poison, damaging blood vessels throughout your body, making them brittle and narrow, restricting vital flow. This can manifest as a persistent thirst, a constant need to urinate, and overwhelming fatigue that drains your very essence. The true terror lies in the devastating complications it unleashes when left unchecked. Think about the agonizing pain of neuropathy, where nerves in your feet and hands can become so damaged that you lose sensation, increasing the risk of unnoticed injuries that can lead to amputation. Consider the devastating impact on your vision, as it can lead to diabetic retinopathy, a leading cause of blindness, turning the world into a hazy, incomprehensible blur. Even your kidneys are at risk, progressively failing until dialysis becomes a life-altering necessity. Beyond the physical toll, diabetes relentlessly chips away at your quality of life and independence. The constant vigilance, the injections, the dietary restrictions – it’s a daily marathon of self-discipline that can feel like an inescapable burden. This chronic condition can breed anxiety and depression, as the fear of future complications looms large, casting a shadow over every aspect of your existence and forcing you to confront a future where even simple pleasures become fraught with risk.", 'terms': ['blood sugar', 'diabetic retino